  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:d85dceec086e5ca5a82000af8c486537207edc83529ab5874ff27b2261b69a4c",
      "text": "In the NINDS NET-PD program, a randomized phase II futility trial of creatine and minocycline (Neurology 2006) found that neither could be rejected as futile and recommended considering both for definitive phase III trials, whereas the later Long-term Study 1 of creatine monohydrate 10 g/d (JAMA 2015; 1741 participants) was terminated early for futility at a planned interim analysis (n = 955) and concluded that creatine did not improve clinical outcomes. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16481597/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4349346/",
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13442935/"
      ],
