    {
      "id": "clm:a2a6125a5af7cb44559e032a06a78c9b38acddbc543f6b49ac15fdc8c2d96077",
      "text": "Two analyses of commercial Mucuna pruriens products reported wide variation in levodopa content: a 2018 HPLC analysis of six products found levodopa content varying from 6% to 141% of label claims with no product within the 90%\u2013110% pharmacopeial limits, and a 2022 JAMA Neurology case series of 16 analyzed supplements found 15 containing levodopa at 2 mg to 241 mg per recommended serving, with actual levodopa 228% to 2186% greater than the estimate for products listing a seed-extract quantity, while carbidopa and benserazide were not detected. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5808387/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9361182/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
