    {
      "id": "clm:f3499cc7ae6ce19c2af1bafd5200f115eac49fb1ceff8b72658e30f24a769fe8",
      "text": "Two coenzyme Q10 (CoQ10) trials in early Parkinson disease reported conflicting results: an eighty-subject dosage-ranging trial (Arch Neurol 2002) reported less functional decline at 1200 mg/d than with placebo (P =.04) and concluded that CoQ10 appears to slow deterioration pending confirmation in a larger study, while the phase III QE3 trial (600 participants; JAMA Neurol 2014) was terminated after a prespecified futility criterion was reached and showed no evidence of clinical benefit; a 2026 review suggests the discrepancies might stem from different sample sizes and study durations. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12374491/",
      "also": [
        "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24664227/",
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13442935/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:041aa7e74f21bcfbf282e0462701d7ef85a3fd9b0e3db20961c4ab8f267f7198",
