    {
      "id": "clm:209dc2f88a4152dc2b39f60a5427157be6fe70e336e9df3cd681a3e95d0e3ce4",
      "text": "In a randomized trial of tocopherol (a component of vitamin E) and deprenyl in early Parkinson's disease (800 patients assigned to placebo, tocopherol, deprenyl or both; N Engl J Med 1993), there was no beneficial effect of tocopherol or any interaction between tocopherol and deprenyl, and a 2026 review likewise reports that no benefits of vitamin E were seen in UPDRS total score. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8417384/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13442935/"
      ],
