    {
      "id": "clm:20be46a889983003ce7e6d7046b618d31c3896e0147939e3bd2bf129e581756e",
      "text": "Sources differ on adverse events with Mucuna pruriens (MP) in Parkinson disease: a 2025 systematic review (5 clinical trials, 108 participants; one study rated high quality, one with some concerns and three low quality) found MP associated with fewer adverse events and no dyskinesia reported while calling current clinical evidence limited, whereas a 12-month open-label phase 2 randomized trial in thirty-two untreated patients reported more frequent adverse events with MP than with levodopa plus a decarboxylase inhibitor (56% vs. 37.5%, p = 0.48; not statistically significant) and stated that larger double-blind trials with extended follow-up of 24\u201336 months are needed. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-27)",
      "source_url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12377966/",
      "also": [
        "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13347555/"
